<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neo-Sumerian Empire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Neo-Sumerian Empire, also known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>, was a Mesopotamian state that emerged around 2112 BCE after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>. Its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur-nammu">Ur-Nammu</a> expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gutians">Gutians</a> and reasserted Sumerian political and cultural identity. The state became known for its highly centralised bureaucracy and record-keeping, and it fell around 2004 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire.jpg" alt="Neo-Sumerian Empire" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Middle_East_topographic_map-blank.svg: Sémhur (talk) derivative work: Zunkir (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ur_III.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
